en Abiah Hezron's wife bare him Ashur the father of Tekoa.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuAnd the sons of Jerahmeel the firstborn of Hezron were, Ram the firstborn, and Bunah, and Oren, and Ozem, and Ahijah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSJerahmeel had also another wife, whose name was Atarah; she was the mother of Onam.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOAnd the sons of Ram the firstborn of Jerahmeel were, Maaz, and Jamin, and Eker.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZAnd the sons of Onam were, Shammai, and Jada. And the sons of Shammai; Nadab, and Abishur.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd the name of the wife of Abishur was Abihail, and she bare him Ahban, and Molid.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJAnd the sons of Nadab; Seled, and Appaim: but Seled died without children.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And the sons of Appaim; Ishi. And the sons of Ishi; Sheshan. And the children of Sheshan; Ahlai.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAnd the sons of Jada the brother of Shammai; Jether, and Jonathan: and Jether died without children.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAnd the sons of Jonathan; Peleth, and Zaza. These were the sons of Jerahmeel.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book§chapter«first_verse"ªlast_verse)¦verses˜„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeNow Sheshan had no sons, but daughters. And Sheshan had a servant, an Egyptian, whose name was Jarha.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd Sheshan gave his daughter to Jarha his servant to wife; and she bare him Attai.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ/And Attai begat Nathan, and Nathan begat Zabad,¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.and Zabad begat Ephlal, and Ephlal begat Obed,¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,and Obed begat Jehu, and Jehu begat Azariah,¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ1and Azariah begat Helez, and Helez begat Eleasah,¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5and Eleasah begat Sisamai, and Sisamai begat Shallum,¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8and Shallum begat Jekamiah, and Jekamiah begat Elishama.¦layout ªlast_verse)…¤book§chapter«first_verse*ªlast_verse1¦verses˜„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–Now the sons of Caleb the brother of Jerahmeel were, Mesha his firstborn, which was the father of Ziph; and the sons of Mareshah the father of Hebron.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAAnd the sons of Hebron; Korah, and Tappuah, and Rekem, and Shema.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFAnd Shema begat Raham, the father of Jorkoam: and Rekem begat Shammai.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEAnd the son of Shammai was Maon: and Maon was the father of Beth-zur.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd Ephah, Caleb's concubine, bare Haran, and Moza, and Gazez: and Haran begat Gazez.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXAnd the sons of Jahdai; Regem, and Jotham, and Gesham, and Pelet, and Ephah, and Shaaph.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ6Maachah, Caleb's concubine, bare Sheber, and Tirhanah.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠShe bare also Shaaph the father of Madmannah, Sheva the father of Machbenah, and the father of Gibea: and the daughter of Caleb was Achsa.¦layout ªlast_verse1…¤book§chapter«first_verse2ªlast_verse7¦verses–„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlThese were the sons of Caleb the son of Hur, the firstborn of Ephratah; Shobal the father of Kirjath-jearim,¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@Salma the father of Beth-lehem, Hareph the father of Beth-gader.¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWAnd Shobal the father of Kirjath-jearim had sons; Haroeh, and half of the Manahethites.¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd the families of Kirjath-jearim; the Ithrites, and the Puhites, and the Shumathites, and the Mishraites; of them came the Zareathites, and the Eshtaulites.¦layout ªlast_verse5„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|The sons of Salma; Beth-lehem, and the Netophathites, Ataroth, the house of Joab, and half of the Manahethites, the Zorites.¦layout ªlast_verse6„¥verse7¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And the families of the scribes which dwelt at Jabez; the Tirathites, the Shimeathites, and Suchathites. These are the Kenites that came of Hemath, the father of the house of Rechab.¦layout ªlast_verse7